{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","fileAccessRequest":false,"metadataBlocks":{"citation":{"displayName":"Citation Metadata","name":"citation","fields":[{"typeName":"title","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Getuigen Verhalen, Vier verzetsvrouwen: Gewoon Doen en Fier Rechtopstaan, interview 01"},{"typeName":"otherId","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"otherIdAgency":{"typeName":"otherIdAgency","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"DANS-KNAW"},"otherIdValue":{"typeName":"otherIdValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"easy-dataset:41258"}}]},{"typeName":"author","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"authorName":{"typeName":"authorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Cultuur & Co."}}]},{"typeName":"datasetContact","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"datasetContactName":{"typeName":"datasetContactName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"a.j  stam"},"datasetContactAffiliation":{"typeName":"datasetContactAffiliation","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"cultuur & co"}}]},{"typeName":"dsDescription","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"dsDescriptionValue":{"typeName":"dsDescriptionValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"<p>Rachel van Amerongen werd geboren in 1914 in Amsterdam.<br>Dit gesprek concentreert zich op  Rachels jeugd en de kennismaking met haar  eerste man Charles Désiré Lu-A-Si, een Surinaamse Nederlander die in juni 1941 is gearresteerd vanwege zijn betrokkenheid bij de februaristaking. De nazi's zetten hem gevangen in Kamp Schoorl. Via Amersfoort, Neuengamme en Dachau werd Charles in Auschwitz gevangen gehouden. Hij overleed daar in november 1942 aan de gevolgen van martelingen.<\/p><p>Rachel is later ook gearresteerd vanwege verzet. Omdat zij Joods was, is zij in Westerbork gevangen gezet. De zoon van Rachel en Charles, Dees, overleefde dankzij o.a. majoor Bosshardt. Rachel overleefde Auschwitz , Bergen-Belsen en Theresienstadt en trok in 1950 met haar tweede man Eddy van Amerongen naar Israël.<\/p>"}}]},{"typeName":"subject","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Arts and Humanities"]},{"typeName":"keyword","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Charles Désiré Lu-A-Si"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Surinamers"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"joden in Amsterdam"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Bijenkorf"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"verzet"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"februaristaking"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"communisten"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Majoor Bosshardt"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"oral history"}},{"keywordValue":{"typeName":"keywordValue","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Tweede Wereldoorlog"}}]},{"typeName":"notesText","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"Er is een minimale edit gedaan door PEPfilm, Pepijn Kortbeek in Amsterdam. Het quicktime bestand bevat nog alle knipjes.  Een copie van dit bestand zal ook bij Aletta, Instituut voor Vrouwengeschiedenis worden gedeponeerd.              \n\nDineke Stam (filmcamera en interviewer), Cultuur & Co"},{"typeName":"language","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Dutch"]},{"typeName":"productionDate","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2009-04-01"},{"typeName":"contributor","multiple":true,"typeClass":"compound","value":[{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"A.J. Stam (Cultuur & Co.)"}},{"contributorName":{"typeName":"contributorName","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"P. Kortbeek (PEPfilm)"}}]},{"typeName":"distributionDate","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2009-12-03"},{"typeName":"dateOfDeposit","multiple":false,"typeClass":"primitive","value":"2009-04-01"},{"typeName":"dataSources","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["Naast de transscriptie van het interview zijn enkele foto's toegevoegd van Rachel wandelend in het huis Beth Juliana (Foto 1 , 4 en 5), een portret (2) en gedurende het interview (3).\n\nRachel van Amerongen is geïnterviewd in het boek en de film van Willy Lindwer: De Laatste Zeven Maanden: Vrouwen in Het Spoor Van Anne Frank. Gooi en Sticht, 1988. ISBN-13: 978-9030404644\n\nDe film van Jon Blair, Anne Frank Remembered bevat ook een interview met Rachel.     \n     \nDe titelpagina van het artikel over Rachels eerste man uit het blad Wi Rutu (2008) is als foto 5 opgenomen.     \n     \nIn 2002 verscheen in Amsterdam een bundel van opstellen geschreven door Rachel's tweede echtgenoot, Eddy van Amerongen (1912-1992), 'Nog slechts herinnering: mijn vooroorlogs Joods Amsterdam'. ISBN: 90 6446 029 9"]}]},"dansRights":{"displayName":"Rights Metadata","name":"dansRights","fields":[{"typeName":"dansRightsHolder","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["Dineke Stam","Bertien Minco"]},{"typeName":"dansPersonalDataPresent","multiple":false,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":"Unknown"},{"typeName":"dansMetadataLanguage","multiple":true,"typeClass":"controlledVocabulary","value":["Dutch"]}]},"dansRelationMetadata":{"displayName":"Relation Metadata","name":"dansRelationMetadata","fields":[{"typeName":"dansAudience","multiple":true,"typeClass":"primitive","value":["https:\/\/www.narcis.nl\/classification\/D34300"],"expandedvalue":[{"@id":"https:\/\